dvapi: add system library path fallback for FHS rootfs

Upstream dvapi.py only searches for libaraclient via DV_TGT_ROOT (SDK
tree layout) or relative to __file__ (../lib/).  Neither works when the
library is installed to a standard FHS path such as /usr/lib/.

Add a final fallback that loads the library by bare SONAME, letting the
system dynamic linker (ld.so) resolve it from the default search paths.
This is the standard ctypes idiom for system-installed shared libraries.

The upstream search order is preserved: DV_TGT_ROOT paths are tried
first, then the relative path, and only then the linker fallback.

--- a/art/linux/aarch64/include/dvapi.py	2026-04-29 19:00:35.334496891 +0300
+++ b/art/linux/aarch64/include/dvapi.py	2026-04-29 19:01:01.590783739 +0300
@@ -92,6 +92,25 @@
             else:
                 lib_loaded = load_dvinfclient_lib(os.path.abspath(os.path.join(cwd,"../lib/libaraclient_aarch64.so")))
       
+    # Fallback: let the dynamic linker find the library via standard paths
+    if not lib_loaded:
+        soname = None
+        if curr_platform == "Linux":
+            os_info = os.uname()
+            if "x86_64" in os_info[4]:
+                soname = "libaraclient_x86_64.so"
+            else:
+                soname = "libaraclient_aarch64.so"
+        elif curr_platform == "Windows":
+            soname = "araclient.dll"
+        if soname:
+            try:
+                DV_API_OBJ = CDLL(soname)
+                logger.info("loaded dvinfclient lib via system linker: %s", soname)
+                lib_loaded = True
+            except OSError:
+                logger.info("failed to load dvinfclient lib via system linker: %s", soname)
+
     if not lib_loaded:
         raise DVClientLibNotFoundError(errno.ENOENT, os.strerror(errno.ENOENT), "unable to load dvinfclient library")
     return DV_API_OBJ
